    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d138">

                <pb facs="0222" n="956" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg956"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Olney to Governor McIntire.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi></placeName>,<lb/><date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1896-01-21"><hi rendition="#italic">January
                                21, 1896</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your letter of the 15th instant, stating the opinions of the attorney-general
                    of Colorado and of the district judge in regard to the Walsenburg lynching, that
                    a grand jury drawn from any other county than Huerfano would not have
                    jurisdiction.</p>
                <p>I have transmitted copies of your letter and its inclosure to the Italian
                    ambassador.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Richard Olney.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
